WEBVTT

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:29.010
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:29.010
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:29.010
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.600 --> 00:02:02.900
Chapter I

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:13.700
In May of Space Year 788,
Imperial Year 479...

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.200
...El Facil Starzone, an outer territory
of the Free Planets Alliance...

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:24.800
...was invaded by an Imperial fleet which
started a battle against its defensive forces.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:32.240
The numbers of both forces
were about 1,000 ships each.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.750
It was considered to be one of the
small-scale skirmishes between the two sides...

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.930
...and they kept attacking and
retreating, with about 20% casualties.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.290
The Imperial Fleet is retreating.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.060
All right.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.690
We'll withdraw, too.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.170
All ships, turn around !

00:02:59.010 --> 00:02:59.910
All ships, turn around !

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:01.880
All ships, turn around !

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.080
Oh, well.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:18.550
When I was young, I never dreamed I'd be here doing something like this.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.700
I guess it's all because of
that accident six years ago.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.300
You want to study
history, you say ?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.230
Yeah.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.700
So I want to take the entrance exam for the History Department of Heinessen Memorial University.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:54.690
Can't you have an interest
in more useful things ?

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.220
What do you mean
"useful things" ?

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.810
Money making and art objects.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:04.380
Money making enriches your wallet,
and art enriches your heart.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.170
Money making, eh ?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.890
Wenli, remember this.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.260
Money is not something
to be despised.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:17.450
If you have money, you don't
have to work for people you hate...

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:21.170
...and you don't have to bend your
principles for the sake of making a living.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.780
It's the same
with politicians...

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:27.200
...we're okay as long as we're firmly in
charge and don't let them get out of control.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.670
Well, I guess it's okay.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.170
It's not like no one has
ever struck gold with history.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.350
Are you saying
it's okay, Dad ?

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:43.610
Thank...

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.070
What happened ?

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:48.600
Captain, this is the engine room.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.000
There's been a problem with
the nuclear fusion reactor.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:51.700
What ?

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:56.370
I'll be there right away.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:58.890
Dad ?

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.350
Just wait here.
I'll talk to you later.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:17.970
Dad !

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:25.170
When the Captain was in the control room trying to cool down the reactor a rapid radiation leak occurred.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.990
The captain closed the
shield on himself, till the end...

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.370
Dad !

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:32.770
Dad !

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.180
Dad...

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:47.350
I'm sorry to inform you, but there are significant liens outstanding against your father's business assets.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:53.500
On balance, his company
is still heavily in debt...

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:59.300
...but your father was supposed to be a master at making money.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:05.800
He owned many works of art. If you sell them, you should still be able to live comfortably.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.950
These are all fakes.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:13.470
All of them ?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.450
That's right, none of this is real.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.480
Are they worth anything ?

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.880
Not even one dinar.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.260
Junk ?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.430
Here's your list...

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.450
...and here's the bill for my services. Payment should be made to the account shown on the bill, please.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.600
This is just
like my father.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:02.250
As you know, because of the
ongoing war with the Empire...

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:05.270
...the budget for education
has been reduced...

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:10.000
...and there aren't many scholarships
available for studies in the humanities.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:13.610
Ah...

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.440
Is there any place where
I could study history for free ?

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.590
Free, huh ?

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:26.470
Oh ?

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:30.440
This is history, isn't it ?

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:31.420
You see ?

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:37.270
Free Planets Alliance Command Academy,
Department of War History Research.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:14.830
Hey !

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.950
Hey, how were your grades ?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:30.750
As always, you're tops in war history research and barely passing in practical training.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:31.650
Huh ?

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.920
Looks like you're in bad shape for
mechanical engineering this time ?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.670
Yeah, I was called
in by my instructor.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.250
He told me I'd have to do well
in the rest of my subjects.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:40.510
The rest of your subjects ?

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.720
You mean strategic
warfare simulation ?

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.170
That's your strong
subject, isn't it ?

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.000
But my opponent is a problem.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.260
Opponent ?

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:48.810
Who is it ?

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.440
It's Wideborn.

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:55.200
Wideborn, you mean the
top student in the class ?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:10.430
Computer, concentrate all forces
and cut off the enemy's supply line.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:15.660
Executed.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.100
We've cut off the
enemy's supply line.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:19.160
Good job.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.160
All forces, retreat !

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:26.810
Look, Yang has withdrawn to his base
and confined himself to defense.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.600
Of course.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.010
He isn't a match for Wideborn.

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:34.100
He is a once-in-a-decade genius.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:37.600
Oh, he's moved his
forces to the left wing.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.040
It's only a matter of time. {that Yang will lose}

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.060
All right !

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.010
There, move our main fleet
and attack their main body !

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.770
The command cannot be executed.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.250
What ?

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:53.560
We are running
short of supplies.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:58.780
If we continue our operation, we will
be out of supplies within three days.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.670
It can't be helped.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.560
We'll withdraw.

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:14.600
Decision - the winner is Yang Wenli.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:25.500
If he fought me straight
out, I would have won !

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.700
He was just
running around !

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:38.200
Cadet Yang, in your third year you are ordered to transfer to the Department of Strategy Research.

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.180
Why ?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:42.900
Can you give me an explanation ?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.170
You're not the only one.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.760
The Department of War History
Research itself will be abolished.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:59.180
All students in this 
department are being transferred.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:03.990
You have the distinction of
defeating Wideborn in simulations.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:07.790
This transfer will be good for you, since it will help develop your natural aptitudes.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:11.480
I enrolled to study war history.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:17.250
To admit students and then
abolish the department, it's...

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:19.610
I don't think it's fair.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:26.650
Cadet Yang, you're not yet in active service,
but when you enrolled in this school...

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:30.560
...you became a member of the armed forces, with the privileges of a junior officer.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.010
While you're in the service,
you must obey orders.

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:39.650
Besides, this isn't
a bad thing for you.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:43.020
The Department of Strategy
Research is full of top students.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:48.000
Students who apply for that department
and fail go to the other departments.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.110
That's the reality.

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:53.800
It's rare for a student to
go in the reverse direction.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.220
I'm honored.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:58.170
But I've never
been a top student.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.040
Don't be sarcastic.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:06.340
Of course, if you don't want to go,
you have the right to say no.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:10.490
But you'll have to repay all
your tuition up to this point.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.450
Only those who become members
of the military get to study for free.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.150
Dad...

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.740
...it's just
like you said.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.130
I never intended
to join the military...

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.110
...but when it rains,
it pours, I guess.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:43.000
Enemy ships are
closing in from behind !

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.680
The enemy ships are returning
to this area quickly !

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:45.910
What ?!

00:12:58.160 --> 00:12:59.250
Why ?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.200
Those Imperial bastards, they
were only pretending to withdraw ?

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.300
Commander, what should we do ?

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.000
Commander !

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.210
Admiral Lynch !

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:10.200
R...retreat.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.160
Retreat ?

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.030
We'll retreat to the
main planet of El Facil !

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:14.400
Hurry !

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.560
But we have to
regroup our fleet first...

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.360
W...we'll regroup after we
return to the main planet !

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.720
For now, we have
to get out of here !

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.170
Hurry !

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:26.510
Hurry !

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:40.940
Fleet Commander Lynch may
have had his own intentions...

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:47.530
...but to his bridge crew it looked like their commander was deserting under fire.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:53.530
The isolated ships which had been fighting
on their own despite their confusion...

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:59.030
...naturally lost their will to fight,
and came about to withdraw from combat.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:06.100
Some ships escaped from the
El Facil Starzone altogether...

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:09.970
...and other ships followed the flagship to
the main planet of the El Facil star system.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:17.400
Those left behind were forced to choose
between a fight to the death or surrender...

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.850
...with most choosing the latter.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:26.850
Despite that...

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:32.850
...the troops that retreated to El Facil
amounted to 200 ships and 50,000 soldiers.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:36.700
Afterwards, the Imperial
force tripled their numbers...

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:40.700
...to take advantage of this
opportunity to seize El Facil...

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.720
...and the fall of El Facil seemed
to be only a matter of time.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:54.700
Approximately 3,000,000
civilians reside on El Facil.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:01.500
They feared the severity of the situation, and rushed to the airports for aid.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:14.600
The Empire claims the righteous cause of liberating people from the "evil" hands of the rebel forces.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:18.500
Therefore, they do
not massacre civilians.

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:23.500
But in the name of rectifying people's
"irrational" belief in republicanism...

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:29.230
...they send the captured people to the
frontiers for forced labor till they die.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:33.800
Fear of that sent the
civilians into a panic.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:47.250
Admiral, the government of
the planet is petitioning for...

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:50.690
...for us to create and implement a plan to evacuate civilians.

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:52.300
What should we do ?

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:54.700
Admiral ?

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.350
It's about the
civilian evacuation plan.

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:02.020
Just find someone with too much
time on his hands and have him do it.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.350
Someone with too much
time on his hands ?

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:22.600
Are you saying you're in
charge of the evacuation plan ?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:27.040
Yes, it seems like
that's the situation.

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:35.250
Hey, will we be okay ?

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:36.630
He's too young.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:37.810
He's a Lieutenant
Junior Grade, right ?

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.370
The rank is too low - can
he be responsible for this ?

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:42.950
Are they serious
about helping us ?

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:47.350
I can hear all that, but...

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.170
...well, I can't blame them.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:17:01.290
Despite people's misgivings,
Yang did what he had to do.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:05.180
Amid the confusion over the
impending attack from the Empire...

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:09.840
...he obtained passenger ships and cargo vessels, and prepared for evacuation.

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:22.700
He's a greenhorn
we can't count on !

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:24.920
He has no track record - how
dare he act like he's so important !

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:36.600
T...thank you, Miss...

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.200
Greenhill.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.700
Frederica Greenhill.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.350
You can call me Frederica.

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.040
Please, Mr. Lieutenant Junior Grade.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:15.380
I don't like coffee.

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.320
I wish you had
given me tea.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.940
Hang in there, Mr. Lieutenant Junior Grade.

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:35.890
Well...

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:56.890
I'm sorry to interrupt, but since I have
prepared an evacuation plan for the civilians...

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:58.180
...I would like to have
you take a look at it.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.290
I'll look at it later.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:01.300
Just leave it on the desk.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:24.650
If it were only the planning of the evacuation,
any competent officer would have done it...

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:27.000
...regardless of whether
he was Yang or not.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:31.900
Calming down the edgy civilians, Yang
seemed to be waiting for an opportune time.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:34.960
Look, the shuttles are...

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:36.660
What ?

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:46.950
What's going to
happen to us ?

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:54.630
LTJG, Admiral Lynch and the other officers at
HQ evacuated along with the military supplies.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:01.050
LTJG Yang, what's going on ?

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:02.240
What's happening here ?

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:04.240
Please calm down.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:08.110
It's only that Admiral Lynch and a
portion of the officers have evacuated.

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:09.450
What ?

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.000
What do you mean "only" ?

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:11.440
Oh, no...

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.990
I was waiting for this.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:17.600
Well, we should
evacuate now, too.

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:20.970
But we'll be going in the opposite
direction of the Admiral and the others.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:26.060
But passenger liners aren't military ships;
they don't even have radar jamming devices.

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:29.690
We'll be found by the Imperial
Fleet in no time, won't we ?

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.210
Oh, please help us.

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.520
There's no need to worry.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:35.920
The Admiral is going to draw
the Imperial Fleet's attention.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:40.320
We don't need to worry about radar;
we can go comfortably riding the solar wind.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:47.300
LTJG Yang, you're using
the Admiral as a decoy ?

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.000
I wish I didn't
need to, but...

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:58.800
Well, please hurry up and get on
the ships, as we already arranged.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:03.420
Yang's prediction was right on.

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:07.250
Rear Admiral Lynch
and the others...

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:10.910
...were found by the Imperial Fleet
who had predicted this outcome...

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.700
...and after being pursued
as if they were being hunted...

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.500
...hoisted the white flag
and became prisoners.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:25.020
In the meantime, the groups of ships
Yang directed evacuated El Facil Starzone.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:29.670
Imperial surveillance spotted them, but...

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:32.280
Picking up some
unidentified objects.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:34.840
No, I don't think so.

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:40.850
Ships that are trying to evacuate would
camouflage themselves from radar somehow.

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:46.780
They're so clearly on the radar;
they must be asteroids or something.

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:48.560
I see.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:53.250
Because of their preconceptions...

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:57.250
...they let an enemy who was so
defenselessly visible escape.

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:01.600
After the Imperial
Fleet found that out...

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:05.800
...it is said that they threw their victory
wine glasses to the floor, mortified.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:10.800
There's nothing more dangerous
than rigid preconceptions.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:16.660
That has been proven at
many junctures of history.

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:22.520
But in the end, humans
repeat the same mistakes.

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:25.980
That's where tricks and ingenuity
become useful, I suppose.

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:30.700
At this time, Yang became
interested in tactics for the first time.

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:33.410
Hey, there he is.

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:36.000
LTJG, thank you.

00:22:36.490 --> 00:22:37.560
We all owe you.

00:22:38.200 --> 00:22:39.870
I believed in you.

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:41.560
Thank you.

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:43.060
You're a hero.

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:53.250
That was the birth
of a great hero.

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:57.270
And this was to become the
starting point for this hero...

00:22:57.270 --> 00:23:01.300
...but there was no one
who knew it at that time.

00:22:58.670 --> 00:23:04.700
The Hero of El Facil

00:23:06.470 --> 00:23:10.300
[ Our Trail ]

00:23:06.470 --> 00:23:10.300
Ending Theme

00:23:06.470 --> 00:23:10.300
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:21.690
Yang:

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:21.690
Goda Hozumi

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:22.260
Without a map, without a compass...

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:27.350
...we set out on a voyage

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:36.700
